**What changed:** `src/queue.ts` now runs jobs strictly one after another in push order via a chained `#tail` promise — each job starts only after the previous one settles, never synchronously inside `push` (which stays synchronous and returns nothing). Thrown errors are caught per job and recorded in `errors` without stopping later jobs. `drain` re-reads `#tail` after each await so it also waits for jobs pushed while draining.

